gaged from beginning to end.From jumping jacks and squats to pretending to be animals, dancing, balancing, and more, every game encourages kids to stay active while practicing important listening and direction-following skills. It’s a wonderful way to burn off energy on rainy days, during indoor recess, as a brain break, or anytime kids need to get their wiggles out.No special equipment is needed, just a little space and a readiness to have fun! If your kids love Simon Says, they’ll have a blast with this movement-filled version that turns exercise into an exciting game they’ll want to play again and again.Run Time: 33 min\n\nLooking for other free audio sources, ideas and inspo? Maybe you want to submit a request for some sort of specific audio for your kids? Join my FB Group! I am always taking suggestions and working to get the audio your kids want.\nToyo Momma Bear source: 3b786deb1866dca76c216c50f1bf0ae6e8650fe4cbc84e24386497f3c34c9b40","abridged":false,"narrators":[],"copyrights":[],"accents":[],"cover":{"imageL":"https://card-content.yotoplay.com/1zqqbCph2mgIoxFuhjAdRyDcVXjke14J9FxcqZmckwuE~/pub/N6LrDAlSNWYk_PQ4-BlBJ5JYq7XLbsUQq2J1db9fx9k"},"authors":["Momma Bear Audio"]}}}